{"Operator rolling-updates feature flag enforcement is absent - UpgradeLogicFactory.create() and RecreateOnImageChangeUpgradeLogic.onUpgrade() never call Profile.isFeatureEnabled(Profile.Feature.ROLLING_UPDATES), meaning rolling updates can occur without the flag despite documentation stating otherwise": 0.5401543378829956, "RECREATE_UPGRADE_EXIT_CODE was silently changed from 4 to 3, with 4 repurposed for FEATURE_DISABLED, breaking existing scripts or automation checking exit code 4 for recreate-required without any migration notice or changelog entry": 0.7908893823623657, "In createInitialDeployment, when updateStrategy == null the method returns early before FeatureSpec is set and ROLLING_UPDATES is added to enabledFeatures, causing parameterized tests with null strategy to deploy Keycloak CR without the rolling-updates feature enabled": 0.7454640865325928, "Rolling update path in KeycloakDeploymentDependentResource.desired() has no feature flag guard - no check for Profile.isFeatureEnabled(Profile.Feature.ROLLING_UPDATES) exists anywhere in the call chain from KeycloakController.reconcile() through to KeycloakDeploymentDependentResource.desired()": 0.48731863498687744, "User-supplied file paths in UpdateCompatibilityCheck and UpdateCompatibilityMetadata are passed directly to new File(...) without canonicalization or base-directory validation, enabling path traversal and arbitrary file writes via mkdirs() on attacker-controlled locations": 0.05194289609789848, "testFeatureNotEnabled does not assert exitCode() == 4 and testWrongVersions does not assert exitCode() == 3, leaving critical exit-code behavioral changes untested": 0.8511428833007812}